The game is long and we take a short break.
We stand together by the court.
I quickly drink some water.
Max, Timo and Lena also drink water.
"Maya, what do you like to do in Berlin?" asks Max.
"I like to ride my bicycle," I answer.
"I like to discover the city."
"And I really like to drink good coffee."
Lena nods and laughs.
"The coffee in Berlin is really good," she says.
"Can you play tennis too?" asks Timo.
I laugh out loud.
"No, I can only play badminton," I say.
"You play really great," says Max.
That pleases me a lot.
We want to play one more game.
The break is over.
We go back onto the court.
